    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_77bc3bd6",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: i'm tired boss; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a photo of a Black man with a weary expression, juxtaposed with text that frames him as a 'boss' who is 'tired of doing time in fb jail because snowflakes get offended over everything.' This visual and textual combination is intended to delegitimize or mock the concept of 'snowflakes' (a term often used pejoratively to describe people perceived as overly sensitive or easily offended). The meme relies on racial stereotyping by using a Black man's image to represent a figure of authority or exhaustion, which can be interpreted as reinforcing harmful tropes that associate Black people with criminality or being 'overly sensitive' in a derogatory way. The overall intent is to express disdain for social media sensitivity, but it does so by leveraging a racialized visual to deliver a message that can be seen as racially charged and potentially harmful to Black individuals and communities.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_641cb3a0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
