      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_80f57fd1",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "The man is mapped as the 'tired boss'",
      "description": "The top text 'i'm tired boss' explicitly maps the visual entity (the Black man with a weary expression) onto the role of 'tired boss'. This is a direct analogical mapping where the textual label 'tired boss' is assigned to the visual person, implying he embodies that role. This mapping is central to the meme's structure and intent, using the visual to represent the textual concept.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_641cb3a0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0cee0ade",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the tired boss scene",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the scene where the Black man with a weary expression is depicted as the 'tired boss'. The meme uses the visual of the man to represent the user's own feelings of exhaustion and frustration with social media dynamics, particularly the perceived over-sensitivity of 'snowflakes'. The text 'i'm tired boss' directly addresses the user, implying that the user identifies with the man's emotional state and role. This projection is reinforced by the overall intent of the meme, which frames the user's experience as one of being overwhelmed by online social conflicts.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_641cb3a0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c11f2165",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Hateful",
      "description": "The meme uses a Black man's image to represent a 'boss' who is 'tired of doing time in fb jail because snowflakes get offended over everything,' which can be interpreted as racially charged and potentially harmful to Black individuals and communities by reinforcing harmful stereotypes that associate Black people with criminality or being 'overly sensitive' in a derogatory way.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_641cb3a0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4728d558",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target audience is individuals who are familiar with internet culture, particularly those who engage with social media platforms like Facebook and understand the term 'snowflakes' as a pejorative. The meme is designed for users who resonate with the sentiment of being overwhelmed by online social dynamics and the perceived hypersensitivity of certain online communities. The use of the 'tired boss' meme template suggests the audience is likely to recognize the visual reference and the cultural context of the phrase, indicating a demographic that is digitally literate and participates in online discourse. The meme's intent to mock 'snowflakes' and 'fb jail' implies the target audience includes those who feel frustrated with social media moderation and the perceived overreaction of online communities, often aligning with users who identify as 'trolls', 'free speech advocates', or 'online skeptics'. The racialized visual of the Black man as the 'boss' may also appeal to an audience that is aware of or engages with racialized internet memes, though this aspect is inherently problematic and potentially alienating to Black audiences.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_641cb3a0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    }
